; Capture by copy (objfpc): function[k, s](x) => e copies k and s when the
; closure is made. It must be a closure (a `reference to` type wanted);
; what it copies must be a variable, a parameter or a field of a type that
; can be copied; the copies are read-only.
; RUN: not %pcc --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/copycapture/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: errors.pas:26:8: error: a lambda that copies what it uses must be a closure: a 'reference to' type must be wanted here
; CHECK: errors.pas:27:17: error: 'items' in the list of what a lambda copies must be of a type that can be copied, not an open or untyped parameter
; CHECK: errors.pas:28:24: error: cannot modify 'n', a copy made by this lambda (copies are read-only)
; CHECK: errors.pas:29:17: error: 'nope' in the list of what a lambda copies must be a variable, a parameter or a field
; CHECK: errors.pas:30:17: error: 'Run' in the list of what a lambda copies must be a variable, a parameter or a field
; CHECK: errors.pas:31:8: error: this lambda has 1 parameter, but 'TFn' is wanted here
; CHECK-NOT: error:
;
; RUN: not %pcc --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/copycapture/syntax.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=SYNTAX %s
; SYNTAX: syntax.pas:8:18: error: expected ']' after the variables a lambda copies
; SYNTAX: syntax.pas:9:17: error: expected name of a variable to copy
;
; The tree: a hidden function $copyN, whose value parameters are the copies
; and whose result is the lambda; the expression calls it.
; RUN: %pcc --mode=objfpc --emit-ast %S/Inputs/copycapture/ast.pas -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=AST %s
; AST: FunctionDecl '$copy2' : TFn <8:8>
; AST-NEXT: ParamDecl 'k' : integer <8:17>
; AST-NEXT: FunctionDecl '$lambda1' : integer <8:8>
; AST: NameRefExpr 'k' parameter : integer <8:32>
; AST: NameRefExpr '$copy2' function result : TFn <8:8>
; AST: CallExpr '$copy2' : TFn <8:8>
; AST-NEXT: NameRefExpr 'k' variable : integer <8:17>
;
; The code: the factory's frame, on the heap, holds the copies.
; RUN: %pcc --mode=objfpc --emit-llvm %S/Inputs/copycapture/ast.pas -o %t.ll
; RUN: FileCheck --check-prefix=IR %s < %t.ll
; RUN: opt -passes=verify -disable-output %t.ll
; IR: call { ptr, ptr } @"pas.$copy2"(ptr null, i32
; IR-LABEL: define internal { ptr, ptr } @"pas.$copy2"(ptr %link, i32 %k)
; IR: call ptr @__pas_frame_new(
